WEBVTT

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:02.016
but that's what you get
for calling me a "ham"

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:03.696
wherever you go.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.197
I remember whenever I'd go
to my grandmother's house,

00:02:06.221 --> 00:02:07.896
she would hide all the photo albums

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.175
because she was afraid of me asking,

00:02:10.199 --> 00:02:11.936
"Well, who is that in that picture?"

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:14.216
and "Who are they to you
and who are they to me,

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:16.576
and how old were you
when that picture was taken?

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.656
How old was I when that picture was taken?

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.496
And why were they in black and white?

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.949
Was the world in black and white
before I was born?"

00:02:22.973 --> 00:02:24.376
DW: Well, that's interesting,

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.736
just to think about the world
in black and white.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:29.096
I grew up in a beauty shop
in North Philadelphia,

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.496
my mom's beauty shop,
looking at "Ebony Magazine,"